2026-11-12:07:09:03 macbookphi2115.win.ad.jhu.edu /Users/pkoehn/LaTex/jhu-intro-hlt.github.io/exam   748  \item[1.] We defined a formal language $\cal{L}$ as a set of strings, where each string is composed of zero or more symbols, each of which is drawn from an alphabet, $\Sigma$.
2026-11-12:07:09:03 macbookphi2115.win.ad.jhu.edu /Users/pkoehn/LaTex/jhu-intro-hlt.github.io/exam   749  \begin{itemize}
