2026-11-12:07:09:03 macbookphi2115.win.ad.jhu.edu /Users/pkoehn/LaTex/jhu-intro-hlt.github.io/exam   750      \item[a.] What is the notation for \emph{all} possible strings drawn from $\Sigma$?\hfill{\em (2 points)}\\\\
2026-11-12:07:09:03 macbookphi2115.win.ad.jhu.edu /Users/pkoehn/LaTex/jhu-intro-hlt.github.io/exam   751      \item[b.] What does $\epsilon$ denote?\hfill{\em (2 points)}\\\\
2026-11-12:07:09:03 macbookphi2115.win.ad.jhu.edu /Users/pkoehn/LaTex/jhu-intro-hlt.github.io/exam   751      \item[b.] What does $\epsilon$ denote?\hfill{\em (2 points)}\\\\
2026-11-12:07:09:03 macbookphi2115.win.ad.jhu.edu /Users/pkoehn/LaTex/jhu-intro-hlt.github.io/exam   752      \item[c.] Define alphabets that could be used for the following languages:
