2026-11-12:07:09:04 macbookphi2115.win.ad.jhu.edu /Users/pkoehn/LaTex/jhu-intro-hlt.github.io/exam   771      \item[b.] Draw a line connecting each remaining item in the \emph{rule format} column with the corresponding entry in the \emph{language class} column.\hfill{\em (4 points)}
2026-11-12:07:09:04 macbookphi2115.win.ad.jhu.edu /Users/pkoehn/LaTex/jhu-intro-hlt.github.io/exam   771      \item[b.] Draw a line connecting each remaining item in the \emph{rule format} column with the corresponding entry in the \emph{language class} column.\hfill{\em (4 points)}
2026-11-12:07:09:04 macbookphi2115.win.ad.jhu.edu /Users/pkoehn/LaTex/jhu-intro-hlt.github.io/exam   772      \item[c.] For the two least powerful language classes (discussed in class), provide an informal example or description of a language that can be captured with rules from that class.\hfill{\em (4 points)}
