2026-11-12:07:09:05 macbookphi2115.win.ad.jhu.edu /Users/pkoehn/LaTex/jhu-intro-hlt.github.io/exam   845  \item What was one of the biggest problems with Recurrent Neural Networks?\hfill{\em (5 points)}
2026-11-12:07:09:05 macbookphi2115.win.ad.jhu.edu /Users/pkoehn/LaTex/jhu-intro-hlt.github.io/exam   846  \solution{Use your best judgment here. What I told them in class (multiple times) was vanishing gradients. They will probably have some pretty good other answers that will be worth points as well.}{\vspace{7cm}}
2026-11-12:07:09:05 macbookphi2115.win.ad.jhu.edu /Users/pkoehn/LaTex/jhu-intro-hlt.github.io/exam   847  \item  Language ID, introduced in the Deep Learning Lecture, is what type of Machine Learning Problem?\hfill{\em (10 points)}
2026-11-12:07:09:05 macbookphi2115.win.ad.jhu.edu /Users/pkoehn/LaTex/jhu-intro-hlt.github.io/exam   848  \solution{I'm looking for ``classification'' and ``supervised learning''. I imagine this will get a range of answers beyond these two. So either of the 2 are correct, plus possibly many more}{\vspace{7cm}}
\item What changed about a decade ago to usher in the era of machine learning? Please only give ONE answer. There are multiple and any ONE that is correct will get full points.\hfill{\em (5 points)}
\solution{I'm looking for either ``size of data'' or ``compute/gpus''. If they give another answer that makes sense, sure. If they give more than one answer, give a 0}{\vspace{7cm}}
2026-11-12:07:09:05 macbookphi2115.win.ad.jhu.edu /Users/pkoehn/LaTex/jhu-intro-hlt.github.io/exam   849  \end{enumerate}
