2026-11-12:07:09:06 macbookphi2115.win.ad.jhu.edu /Users/pkoehn/LaTex/jhu-intro-hlt.github.io/exam   854  \item Why are cross-encoders usually only used as rerankers? 
2026-11-12:07:09:06 macbookphi2115.win.ad.jhu.edu /Users/pkoehn/LaTex/jhu-intro-hlt.github.io/exam   855  \hfill{\em (2 points)}
2026-11-12:07:09:06 macbookphi2115.win.ad.jhu.edu /Users/pkoehn/LaTex/jhu-intro-hlt.github.io/exam   856  \solution{Because the documents cannot be preprocessed or indexed like bi-encoders do.}{\vspace{4cm}}
2026-11-12:07:09:06 macbookphi2115.win.ad.jhu.edu /Users/pkoehn/LaTex/jhu-intro-hlt.github.io/exam   856  \solution{Because the documents cannot be preprocessed or indexed like bi-encoders do.}{\vspace{4cm}}
2026-11-12:07:09:06 macbookphi2115.win.ad.jhu.edu /Users/pkoehn/LaTex/jhu-intro-hlt.github.io/exam   856  \solution{Because the documents cannot be preprocessed or indexed like bi-encoders do.}{\vspace{4cm}}
2026-11-12:07:09:06 macbookphi2115.win.ad.jhu.edu /Users/pkoehn/LaTex/jhu-intro-hlt.github.io/exam   857  \item What is the common approach for creating a numerical value for pointwise ranking using a generative model?
2026-11-12:07:09:06 macbookphi2115.win.ad.jhu.edu /Users/pkoehn/LaTex/jhu-intro-hlt.github.io/exam   858  \hfill{\em (3 points)}
2026-11-12:07:09:06 macbookphi2115.win.ad.jhu.edu /Users/pkoehn/LaTex/jhu-intro-hlt.github.io/exam   859  \solution{
2026-11-12:07:09:06 macbookphi2115.win.ad.jhu.edu /Users/pkoehn/LaTex/jhu-intro-hlt.github.io/exam   860  Take the softmax between the probability of generating yes over no (or any other reasonable pairs). 
2026-11-12:07:09:06 macbookphi2115.win.ad.jhu.edu /Users/pkoehn/LaTex/jhu-intro-hlt.github.io/exam   861  Other acceptable answers could be (a) training a head/pooler on the (last) hidden states to produce a numerical score, or (b) prompting the model to give a graded rating. 
2026-11-12:07:09:06 macbookphi2115.win.ad.jhu.edu /Users/pkoehn/LaTex/jhu-intro-hlt.github.io/exam   862  However, since option (b) is likely to produce many ties among the candidate documents, this answer can only receive 2 points. 
2026-11-12:07:09:06 macbookphi2115.win.ad.jhu.edu /Users/pkoehn/LaTex/jhu-intro-hlt.github.io/exam   863  }{\vspace{4cm}}
2026-11-12:07:09:06 macbookphi2115.win.ad.jhu.edu /Users/pkoehn/LaTex/jhu-intro-hlt.github.io/exam   863  }{\vspace{4cm}}
2026-11-12:07:09:06 macbookphi2115.win.ad.jhu.edu /Users/pkoehn/LaTex/jhu-intro-hlt.github.io/exam   864  \item What are the essential ingredients for using Cranfield evaluation?  
2026-11-12:07:09:06 macbookphi2115.win.ad.jhu.edu /Users/pkoehn/LaTex/jhu-intro-hlt.github.io/exam   865  \hfill{\em (3 points)}
2026-11-12:07:09:06 macbookphi2115.win.ad.jhu.edu /Users/pkoehn/LaTex/jhu-intro-hlt.github.io/exam   866  \solution{A fixed document collection (1 point), a set of topics/queries (1 point), and relevance judgments/labels for a subset of documents for each topic (1 point).}{\vspace{4cm}}
2026-11-12:07:09:06 macbookphi2115.win.ad.jhu.edu /Users/pkoehn/LaTex/jhu-intro-hlt.github.io/exam   866  \solution{A fixed document collection (1 point), a set of topics/queries (1 point), and relevance judgments/labels for a subset of documents for each topic (1 point).}{\vspace{4cm}}
2026-11-12:07:09:06 macbookphi2115.win.ad.jhu.edu /Users/pkoehn/LaTex/jhu-intro-hlt.github.io/exam   867  \item Why is retrieval still important for LLM assistant systems? 
2026-11-12:07:09:06 macbookphi2115.win.ad.jhu.edu /Users/pkoehn/LaTex/jhu-intro-hlt.github.io/exam   868  \hfill{\em (2 points)}
2026-11-12:07:09:06 macbookphi2115.win.ad.jhu.edu /Users/pkoehn/LaTex/jhu-intro-hlt.github.io/exam   869  \solution{Because the generation model has limitations in knowledge, particularly events after the model was trained (1 point), and retrieval provides grounded information for improving the trustworthiness of the system output (1 point).}{\vspace{4cm}}
2026-11-12:07:09:06 macbookphi2115.win.ad.jhu.edu /Users/pkoehn/LaTex/jhu-intro-hlt.github.io/exam   869  \solution{Because the generation model has limitations in knowledge, particularly events after the model was trained (1 point), and retrieval provides grounded information for improving the trustworthiness of the system output (1 point).}{\vspace{4cm}}
