2026-11-12:07:09:06 macbookphi2115.win.ad.jhu.edu /Users/pkoehn/LaTex/jhu-intro-hlt.github.io/exam   873  \Question{\Large Large Language Models}{10}
2026-11-12:07:09:06 macbookphi2115.win.ad.jhu.edu /Users/pkoehn/LaTex/jhu-intro-hlt.github.io/exam   874  You want to build a sentiment detection model (i.e., determining if a text's sentiment is either positive or negative) using either a BERT-style model or a Large Languege Model (LLM).
2026-11-12:07:09:06 macbookphi2115.win.ad.jhu.edu /Users/pkoehn/LaTex/jhu-intro-hlt.github.io/exam   875  \begin{enumerate}
2026-11-12:07:09:06 macbookphi2115.win.ad.jhu.edu /Users/pkoehn/LaTex/jhu-intro-hlt.github.io/exam   876  \item What data do you need to set this up as a supervised learning task?\hfill{\em (2 points)}
2026-11-12:07:09:06 macbookphi2115.win.ad.jhu.edu /Users/pkoehn/LaTex/jhu-intro-hlt.github.io/exam   877  \solution{Text with annotation as positive/negative}{\vspace{2cm}}
2026-11-12:07:09:06 macbookphi2115.win.ad.jhu.edu /Users/pkoehn/LaTex/jhu-intro-hlt.github.io/exam   878  \item How would you build such a model based on a pre-existing BERT-style model? Provide some details about the model architecture of your added components.\\ \phantom{x}\hfill{\em (4~points)}
2026-11-12:07:09:06 macbookphi2115.win.ad.jhu.edu /Users/pkoehn/LaTex/jhu-intro-hlt.github.io/exam   879  \solution{Encode the text with the BERT model, and then add a custom classifier, such as a max-pooling layer, followed by a number of feed-forward layers.}{\vspace{4cm}}
2026-11-12:07:09:06 macbookphi2115.win.ad.jhu.edu /Users/pkoehn/LaTex/jhu-intro-hlt.github.io/exam   880  \item How would you use a Large Language Model to handle this task? Name at least three methods that you may deploy.\hfill{\em (4 points)}
2026-11-12:07:09:06 macbookphi2115.win.ad.jhu.edu /Users/pkoehn/LaTex/jhu-intro-hlt.github.io/exam   881  \solution{In-context learning: describe the task to the LLM. Few-shot learning: provide examples in prompt. Fine-tune the model.}{\vspace{4cm}}
2026-11-12:07:09:06 macbookphi2115.win.ad.jhu.edu /Users/pkoehn/LaTex/jhu-intro-hlt.github.io/exam   882  \end{enumerate}
2026-11-12:07:09:06 macbookphi2115.win.ad.jhu.edu /Users/pkoehn/LaTex/jhu-intro-hlt.github.io/exam   882  \end{enumerate}
