2026-11-12:07:09:06 macbookphi2115.win.ad.jhu.edu /Users/pkoehn/LaTex/jhu-intro-hlt.github.io/exam   885  \Question{\Large Preference Training}{15}
2026-11-12:07:09:06 macbookphi2115.win.ad.jhu.edu /Users/pkoehn/LaTex/jhu-intro-hlt.github.io/exam   886  You want to build a short story generation bot with the help of a Large Language Model. You want the stories to be engaging, creative, and have a twist. Your plan is to use reinforcement learning with human feedback.
2026-11-12:07:09:06 macbookphi2115.win.ad.jhu.edu /Users/pkoehn/LaTex/jhu-intro-hlt.github.io/exam   887  \begin{enumerate}
2026-11-12:07:09:06 macbookphi2115.win.ad.jhu.edu /Users/pkoehn/LaTex/jhu-intro-hlt.github.io/exam   888  \item You have access to human annotators. What will you ask them to do?\hfill{\em (4 points)}
2026-11-12:07:09:06 macbookphi2115.win.ad.jhu.edu /Users/pkoehn/LaTex/jhu-intro-hlt.github.io/exam   889  \solution{Rate stories generated by the model using the three criteria.}{\vspace{4cm}}
2026-11-12:07:09:06 macbookphi2115.win.ad.jhu.edu /Users/pkoehn/LaTex/jhu-intro-hlt.github.io/exam   890  \item What model will you train with the human-annotated data?
2026-11-12:07:09:06 macbookphi2115.win.ad.jhu.edu /Users/pkoehn/LaTex/jhu-intro-hlt.github.io/exam   891  \hfill{\em (3 points)}
2026-11-12:07:09:06 macbookphi2115.win.ad.jhu.edu /Users/pkoehn/LaTex/jhu-intro-hlt.github.io/exam   892  \solution{Reward/Preference model.}{\vspace{4cm}}
2026-11-12:07:09:06 macbookphi2115.win.ad.jhu.edu /Users/pkoehn/LaTex/jhu-intro-hlt.github.io/exam   893  \item You will be using Direct Preference Optimization. The formula for this is:
2026-11-12:07:09:06 macbookphi2115.win.ad.jhu.edu /Users/pkoehn/LaTex/jhu-intro-hlt.github.io/exam   894  \begin{equation*}
2026-11-12:07:09:07 macbookphi2115.win.ad.jhu.edu /Users/pkoehn/LaTex/jhu-intro-hlt.github.io/exam   895  \text{Loss}(x,y_w,y_l) = \log \text{sigmoid} \Big( \beta \log \frac{\pi_\theta(y_w|x)}{\pi_\text{ref}(y_w|x)} - \beta \log \frac{\pi_\theta(y_l|x)}{\pi_\text{ref}(y_l|x)} \Big)
2026-11-12:07:09:07 macbookphi2115.win.ad.jhu.edu /Users/pkoehn/LaTex/jhu-intro-hlt.github.io/exam   896  \end{equation*}
2026-11-12:07:09:07 macbookphi2115.win.ad.jhu.edu /Users/pkoehn/LaTex/jhu-intro-hlt.github.io/exam   897  Explain in a sentence each, what the terms in this equation refer to, given your setup.\\ \phantom{x}\hfill{\em (8 points)}
2026-11-12:07:09:07 macbookphi2115.win.ad.jhu.edu /Users/pkoehn/LaTex/jhu-intro-hlt.github.io/exam   898  \begin{enumerate}\itemsep 10mm
2026-11-12:07:09:07 macbookphi2115.win.ad.jhu.edu /Users/pkoehn/LaTex/jhu-intro-hlt.github.io/exam   899      \item $y_w$: \solution{Story that the reward model prefers}{}
2026-11-12:07:09:07 macbookphi2115.win.ad.jhu.edu /Users/pkoehn/LaTex/jhu-intro-hlt.github.io/exam   900      \item $y_l$: \solution{Story that the reward model disprefers}{}
2026-11-12:07:09:07 macbookphi2115.win.ad.jhu.edu /Users/pkoehn/LaTex/jhu-intro-hlt.github.io/exam   901      \item $\pi_\theta$: \solution{The adapted LLM you are training}{}
2026-11-12:07:09:07 macbookphi2115.win.ad.jhu.edu /Users/pkoehn/LaTex/jhu-intro-hlt.github.io/exam   902      \item $\pi_\text{ref}$: \solution{The original LLM}{}
2026-11-12:07:09:07 macbookphi2115.win.ad.jhu.edu /Users/pkoehn/LaTex/jhu-intro-hlt.github.io/exam   903  \end{enumerate}
2026-11-12:07:09:07 macbookphi2115.win.ad.jhu.edu /Users/pkoehn/LaTex/jhu-intro-hlt.github.io/exam   904  \end{enumerate}
